    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=\\frac{5^3}{x^2}$, with $x>0$ and $y>0$.\n\nCombine logarithms using the power and product laws, then exponentiate base 5.",
      "worked": "For $x>0$ and $y>0$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_5 y&=3-\\log_5 x^2\\\\\\log_5 y+\\log_5 x^2&=3\\\\\\log_5(yx^2)&=3\\\\yx^2&=5^3\\\\y&=\\frac{5^3}{x^2}\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 35
  },
